Fixes product url rewrites receiving the url_key of a different store view during product import.

Symptom: after an import, url_rewrite.request_path for a store view no longer matches that store
view's own url_key in catalog_product_entity_varchar. Every store view of the product ends up with
one identical request_path, taken from the default scope value. On a multi-language setup this makes
a store view serve another language's URL, e.g. a French request_path answering on a German store.
The url_key values in EAV stay correct, only url_rewrite is wrong, which makes the problem look like
a data issue when it is not.

Root cause: AfterImportDataObserver::$cachedValues holds the store-scoped url_key values used by
getReqPath() to correct the request_path of products that were populated from a default-scope import
row (populateGlobalProduct() puts a single shared product object into the slot of every store view of
every website the product is assigned to). The property is filled in initializeCacheForProducts()
only when it is still null, and it is never reset. The observer is a DI singleton and execute() runs
once per import bunch, so from the second bunch onwards the cache still holds the first bunch's
products. isset($this->cachedValues[$productId][$storeId]) is then false for every later product and
getReqPath() falls back to the shared default-scope product's url_key, writing it to all store views.

Fix: reset $this->cachedValues to null at the end of generateUrls(), next to the existing
$this->productCategories reset, so each bunch recomputes the scope-based url_key values for its own
products. This is the behaviour the surrounding code already assumes.

Reproduced by the integration test
vendor/creativestyle/customization-rieker-staging/Test/Integration/UrlRewrite/ImportUrlRewriteScopeTest.php
which is red without this patch and green with it.

diff --git a/Observer/AfterImportDataObserver.php b/Observer/AfterImportDataObserver.php
index a2276ce..a9c1dec 100644
--- a/Observer/AfterImportDataObserver.php
+++ b/Observer/AfterImportDataObserver.php
@@ -446,6 +446,7 @@ class AfterImportDataObserver implements ObserverInterface
         }
         $mergeDataProvider->merge($this->currentUrlRewritesRegenerate($products));
         $this->productCategories = null;
+        $this->cachedValues = null;
         return $mergeDataProvider->getData();
     }

